{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015K4z5LBmbi7dgsTKvr2vBG","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 74134b4eb2030e75fd5b450c4cfc8eb9c8c61f4b\nAuthor: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>\nDate:   Sat Apr 11 01:06:00 2026 +0200\n\n    perf: batch Round 0 coset-parallel kernel launches\n    \n    Batch ~935 sequential small coset-parallel kernel launches in Round 0\n    (zerocheck + logup) into 2 batched kernel launches using per-AIR\n    metadata structs. Each batched kernel processes all small AIRs\n    (GLOBAL=false, buffer_size <= 16) simultaneously via a 2D grid\n    (total_x_blocks, max_num_cosets) with air_for_block mapping.\n    \n    CUDA changes:\n    - Add ZerocheckBatchMeta/LogupBatchMeta structs\n    - Add batched evaluation kernels derived from existing coset-parallel\n      kernels, using blockIdx.x -> per-AIR metadata lookup\n    - Add extern \"C\" launcher functions that dispatch evaluation kernel\n      + batched_final_reduce_block_sums reduction\n    \n    Rust orchestration:\n    - Classify AIRs as batch-eligible vs individual in Phase 1\n    - Collect per-AIR metadata and issue batched launches in sub-phase B\n    - Extract per-AIR results from flat output buffers in Phase 2\n    - Memory budget check (128 MB) disables batching when skip_domain\n      is large to prevent GPU OOM\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n .../cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu       | 206 ++++++++++\n .../cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu   | 200 +++++++++\n crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs    |  82 ++++\n crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs     | 457 ++++++++++++++++++---\n crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs  |  58 +++\n 5 files changed, 953 insertions(+), 50 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b77fa94-4d5e-48a3-b9a0-48eea84a6b29","uuid":"8fad144d-c026-48a7-adab-3f42f1251f7c","timestamp":"2026-04-11T08:56:02.094Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit 74134b4eb2030e75fd5b450c4cfc8eb9c8c61f4b\nAuthor: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>\nDate:   Sat Apr 11 01:06:00 2026 +0200\n\n    perf: batch Round 0 coset-parallel kernel launches\n    \n    Batch ~935 sequential small coset-parallel kernel launches in Round 0\n    (zerocheck + logup) into 2 batched kernel launches using per-AIR\n    metadata structs. Each batched kernel processes all small AIRs\n    (GLOBAL=false, buffer_size <= 16) simultaneously via a 2D grid\n    (total_x_blocks, max_num_cosets) with air_for_block mapping.\n    \n    CUDA changes:\n    - Add ZerocheckBatchMeta/LogupBatchMeta structs\n    - Add batched evaluation kernels derived from existing coset-parallel\n      kernels, using blockIdx.x -> per-AIR metadata lookup\n    - Add extern \"C\" launcher functions that dispatch evaluation kernel\n      + batched_final_reduce_block_sums reduction\n    \n    Rust orchestration:\n    - Classify AIRs as batch-eligible vs individual in Phase 1\n    - Collect per-AIR metadata and issue batched launches in sub-phase B\n    - Extract per-AIR results from flat output buffers in Phase 2\n    - Memory budget check (128 MB) disables batching when skip_domain\n      is large to prevent GPU OOM\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n .../cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu       | 206 ++++++++++\n .../cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu   | 200 +++++++++\n crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs    |  82 ++++\n crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs     | 457 ++++++++++++++++++---\n crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs  |  58 +++\n 5 files changed, 953 insertions(+), 50 deletions(-)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
